# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — reunion-solar-analysis
# =============================================================================
# This repository follows a fully automated, reproducible pipeline: scripts
# 01 -> 03 regenerate everything in outputs/ from the data in data/. Pipeline
# outputs are therefore NOT version-controlled — they are reproducible
# artifacts, not source material. Static copies of the two final maps used
# in this README live separately in figures/, which IS tracked (see below).
#
#   - data/raster/    TRACKED    GHI raster, Global Solar Atlas 3.0
#                                (World Bank Group / Solargis) — CC BY 4.0,
#                                redistribution explicitly permitted with
#                                attribution. Already reprojected to
#                                EPSG:2975 in QGIS prior to being committed
#                                (see README, "Methodology and scripts").
#
#   - data/vectors/   NOT TRACKED for the shapefile itself. The commune
#                                boundary layer (REU_adm2.shp and sidecars)
#                                is GADM v2.8 (Hijmans, 2015; UC Berkeley
#                                Museum of Vertebrate Zoology / International
#                                Rice Research Institute; Stanford Digital
#                                Repository, https://purl.stanford.edu/pn417fx4462).
#                                Its license states: "Redistribution, or
#                                commercial use is not allowed without prior
#                                permission." Committing this file to a public
#                                repository would constitute redistribution.
#                                Only data/vectors/README.md (download
#                                instructions + citation) is tracked; each
#                                user retrieves the shapefile independently
#                                under the dataset's own academic-use terms.
#
#   - figures/        TRACKED    Static copies of the two final maps
#                                (Final_GHI_Distribution_Map.png,
#                                Optimal_Solar_Zones.png), embedded directly
#                                in README.md for visual preview on GitHub,
#                                plus the island location figure. These are
#                                a snapshot for documentation purposes, not
#                                regenerated automatically — refresh them
#                                manually from outputs/maps/ if the pipeline
#                                output changes.
#
#   - outputs/maps/   NOT TRACKED  Maps regenerated by scripts 02 and 03.
#   - outputs/tables/ NOT TRACKED  Summary statistics (CSV) regenerated by
#                                  scripts 02 and 03.
#
# Rerunning scripts/01 -> 03 locally reproduces everything under outputs/
# from data/ — that reproducibility is the point of not tracking it.
# =============================================================================

# --- Non-redistributable vector data (GADM v2.8 license restriction) -------
# See data/vectors/README.md for the official download link.
data/vectors/REU_adm2.*
!data/vectors/README.md

# --- Pipeline outputs (regenerated by scripts/01 -> 03) ---------------------
outputs/maps/
outputs/tables/
!outputs/maps/.gitkeep
!outputs/tables/.gitkeep

# --- Python virtual environments --------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.conda/

# --- Python caches and compiled files ---------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# --- Jupyter / Spyder --------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.spyproject/
.spyderworkspace

# --- IDE / editors -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- OS-specific files --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Temporary files and logs -------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# Safety net: 03_optimal_zones.py now vectorizes the thresholded raster
# directly in memory (rasterio.features.shapes on the numpy array + its
# affine transform), so no intermediate .tif is written to disk anymore.
# Rule kept in case a future change reintroduces a temporary raster file.
ghi_zone_temp.tif
outputs/maps/ghi_zone_temp.tif

# --- Credentials / secrets (security) ------------------------------------------
.env
*.pem
secrets.yaml